{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-tsx","path":"/posts/2015-06-09---Quick-Tip-Getting-A-Variables-Data-During-Debugging/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"id":"b31adc80-24fa-5350-a2ee-da45dbf4211c","html":"<p>Ever wanted a quick overview of an element in debug mode? If you want to know a value a couple of layers deep, you soon have something like this:</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 642px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/1bba8/layereddebuginfo.png\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 56.25%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/8ac56/layereddebuginfo.webp 240w,\n/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/d3be9/layereddebuginfo.webp 480w,\n/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/7eb86/layereddebuginfo.webp 642w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 642px) 100vw, 642px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/8ff5a/layereddebuginfo.png 240w,\n/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/e85cb/layereddebuginfo.png 480w,\n/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/1bba8/layereddebuginfo.png 642w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 642px) 100vw, 642px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/ca81bb322632bb643aef6642aa290496/1bba8/layereddebuginfo.png\"\n            alt=\"Debug layers\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>This poses several annoyances:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>You have to keep your mouse within boundaries.</li>\n<li>It obstructs your code.</li>\n<li>You have to scroll to see all properties.</li>\n<li>You can’t do anything else.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>An alternative which I very much like is <code class=\"language-text\">?</code>. That’s right, a simple question mark. Use this in combination with your immediate window and it will print out all the data you normally get from hovering. For example as you can see in the image below: <code class=\"language-text\">?_affectedProperties</code> will show me the string representation of the list. I can also use more complicated expressions like <code class=\"language-text\">?_affectedProperties.ElementAt(0)</code> to get the detailed info of deeper layers.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 960px; \"\n    >\n      <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 74.58333333333333%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/png;base64,'); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <picture>\n          <source\n              srcset=\"/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/8ac56/questionmarkimwind.webp 240w,\n/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/d3be9/questionmarkimwind.webp 480w,\n/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/e46b2/questionmarkimwind.webp 960w,\n/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/c18de/questionmarkimwind.webp 1052w\"\n              sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n              type=\"image/webp\"\n            />\n          <source\n            srcset=\"/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/8ff5a/questionmarkimwind.png 240w,\n/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/e85cb/questionmarkimwind.png 480w,\n/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/d9199/questionmarkimwind.png 960w,\n/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/218a4/questionmarkimwind.png 1052w\"\n            sizes=\"(max-width: 960px) 100vw, 960px\"\n            type=\"image/png\"\n          />\n          <img\n            class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n            src=\"/static/f11d64465dc39b6cf86e11b57c135fb7/d9199/questionmarkimwind.png\"\n            alt=\"Immediate Window\"\n            title=\"\"\n            loading=\"lazy\"\n            decoding=\"async\"\n            style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n          />\n        </picture>\n    </span>\nAlso worth mentioning is <a href=\"https://marketplace.visualstudio.com/items?itemName=OmarElabd.ObjectExporter\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow noopener noreferrer\">Object Exporter</a> which is an extension that does this for you.</p>","fields":{"slug":"/posts/2015-06-09---Quick-Tip-Getting-A-Variables-Data-During-Debugging/","tagSlugs":["/tag/c/","/tag/debugging/","/tag/visual-studio/"]},"frontmatter":{"date":"2015-06-09T00:00:00.000Z","tags":["C#","Debugging","Visual Studio"],"title":"Quick Tip: Getting a variable's data during debugging","description":"Ever wanted a quick overview of an element in debug mode?","socialImage":null}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/posts/2015-06-09---Quick-Tip-Getting-A-Variables-Data-During-Debugging/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["4208939363"],"slicesMap":{}}